.TH CDSSWARM "1" "2026\-02\-25" "cdsswarm 0.1.5" "cdsswarm Manual"
.SH NAME
cdsswarm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cdsswarm
[-h] [--version] [-w WORKERS] [-m {interactive,script,auto}] [--no-skip] [--resume | --no-resume] [--reuse | --no-reuse] [--max-retries MAX_RETRIES] [--output-dir OUTPUT_DIR] [--dry-run] [--ignore-warnings] [--log FILE] [--summary FILE] [--post-hook CMD] requests_file
.SH DESCRIPTION
Concurrent CDS API downloader with TUI

.TP
\fBrequests_file\fR
JSON or YAML file with download requests

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit

.TP
\fB\-w\fR \fI\,WORKERS\/\fR, \fB\-\-workers\fR \fI\,WORKERS\/\fR
Number of parallel download workers (default: 4)

.TP
\fB\-m\fR \fI\,{interactive,script,auto}\/\fR, \fB\-\-mode\fR \fI\,{interactive,script,auto}\/\fR
Display mode (default: auto)

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-skip\fR
Re\-download files that already exist

.TP
\fB\-\-resume\fR, \fB\-\-no\-resume\fR
Resume interrupted session if state file exists (default: enabled)

.TP
\fB\-\-reuse\fR, \fB\-\-no\-reuse\fR
Reuse existing CDS jobs with matching parameters (default: enabled)

.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI\,MAX_RETRIES\/\fR
Max retry attempts per task (default: 3, 1 to disable)

.TP
\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fI\,OUTPUT_DIR\/\fR
Prepend directory to relative target paths

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be downloaded without actually downloading

.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-warnings\fR
Auto\-continue on warnings without prompting

.TP
\fB\-\-log\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Write timestamped log to FILE

.TP
\fB\-\-summary\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Export summary as JSON (.json) or CSV (.csv)

.TP
\fB\-\-post\-hook\fR \fI\,CMD\/\fR
Shell command to run after each successful download. Placeholders: {file} (output path), {dataset} (dataset name)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
The following subcommands are available.
Run \fBcdsswarm \fISUBCOMMAND\fB \-\-help\fR for full usage.
.SS cdsswarm generate
Expand a template into a request file
.P
Synopsis: \fBcdsswarm generate\fR [\-\-split\-by \fIFIELDS\fR] [\-o \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-dry\-run] \fItemplate_file\fR
.TP
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fItemplate_file\fR
Path to template JSON/YAML file
.TP
\fB--split-by\fR
Comma\-separated split fields (overrides template's split_by)
.TP
\fB-o\fR, \fB--output\fR \fIFILE\fR
Output file path (default: stdout)
.TP
\fB--dry-run\fR
Show task count and targets without writing output
.SS cdsswarm cancel
Cancel active CDS API requests
.P
Synopsis: \fBcdsswarm cancel\fR [\-y] [\fIrequest_id\fR ...]
.TP
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fIrequest_ids\fR
Specific request IDs to cancel (omit to cancel all active)
.TP
\fB-y\fR, \fB--yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompt
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are resolved in order: CLI flags > config file > defaults.
The config file is \fB.cdsswarm.toml\fR in the current directory or any parent.
See the project README for all available keys.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
All downloads completed successfully.
.TP
\fB1\fR
One or more downloads failed, or the run was cancelled.
